name w2-02-ingress
timeout 1700
time 1981-06-07T12:55:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W2, SORTIE 2 OF 10 - OSIRAK 1981 (OPERATION OPERA): REACH, NOT COMBAT.
# THE LOW-LEVEL INGRESS, AND THE [DISPUTED] ALTITUDE THAT DECIDES WHAT KIND OF PROBLEM THIS IS.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w2-osirak.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none, and it is the control of nothing. It stands alone.
#
# THE ANCHOR, AND ITS OWN DISAGREEMENT WITH ITSELF. The ingress altitude is [DISPUTED] and neither
# value is preferred: Wikipedia says the package crossed at 30 m [T4]; Defence Aviation says 240 m
# [T4]. A FACTOR OF EIGHT, and the spec says plainly what hangs on it - at 30 m the raid is a
# terrain-following problem and at 240 m it is an ordinary low-level leg. THIS FILE FLIES 240 m AND
# STATES WHY THE OTHER VALUE IS NOT FLOWN, rather than averaging two sources into a number neither of
# them published.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: CAN THE GUIDANCE HOLD THE INGRESS ALTITUDE OVER A 300 km LEG AT ALL, AND
# WHAT IS THE MARGIN AGAINST THE GROUND THAT IS REALLY THERE? Two numbers, and they come from
# different places on purpose: the altitude-hold spread out of THIS run's `altM` column, and the real
# terrain under the route out of the elevation provider (below).
#
# WHY 30 m IS NOT FLYABLE HERE, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED (`C20`). `FBNavSystem`'s `Direct` holds
# an ALTITUDE ABOVE THE DATUM, not a height above the ground; there is no terrain-following guidance
# and none is approximated. The real ground under this route was MEASURED off `fb-tiles` /elev, warmed
# and read point by point:
#   Etzion   29.94000 34.87000   523.59 m      31.50/39.50   865.62 m
#   30.20/35.50            1,599.22 m          32.00/41.00   622.15 m
#   30.50/36.50              896.99 m          32.50/42.50   301.25 m
#   31.00/38.00              578.06 m          33.00/44.00    42.83 m
#                                              the dome        46.70 m
# A 30 m ASL leg over that ground is between 13 m and 1,569 m UNDERGROUND, and a 240 m ASL leg is
# between 193 m underground and 1,359 m underground for most of it. The campaign is therefore flown
# under `--elev const` on a 0 m plane, where 240 m ASL IS 240 m AGL - and that flat plane is the only
# reason the anchor's lower altitude is expressible at all. TWO ATTRIBUTION RUNS SAY WHAT THAT COSTS
# and are recorded in the campaign file's §State, not here.
#
# THE ARENA: the last 300.0 km of the raid's inbound track, bearing 068.37 deg, from 32.20668 41.54287
# (300 km short of the dome, over the western Iraqi desert) to the reactor site. Scale as in every W2
# file: 1 deg lat = 111,320 m, 1 deg lon at 31.570 N = 94,845 m [DERIVED].
#   `w2van`  target_soft  33.20000 44.52000 - a radar van at the site, the object at the leg's end
#                         (campaign rule 3: a leg with nothing to hit at its end measures nothing)
#
# THE SIX STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES OF THIS CAMPAIGN, in short form (full text in w2-01-dome.fbm):
#   1. `C5` half closed - `tank370` exists, AERIAL REFUELLING DOES NOT and is not approximated. This
#      sortie flies CLEAN, so it measures the ingress and says nothing about the tanks.
#   2. `C20` open, `--elev const`, 0 m plane - the subject of this very file, measured above.
#   3. `C10` - the delivery is a level laydown, no dive and no pop-up.
#   4. `C7` - no F-15; irrelevant here, nothing is hostile in the air.
#   5. `FirstFlightKo` - irrelevant here, one aircraft.
#   6. W1's fixed point - irrelevant here, no air-to-air.
# And the campaign-wide fuel discipline: `set fuel_int_pct`, never `set fuel_pct`.
#
# READING RULE (binding): the exit code is NOT the measurement. Read, in this order: (1) the spread of
# the `altM` column over the whole leg against the declared 240 m, (2) `aglM` beside it - under
# `--elev const` the two are the same number, which is the disclosure and not a result, (3)
# `stores DELIVERY aimErrM` and the van's `UNIT_RESULT`, (4) `fuelLbs` in the last row, against
# w2-03's clean 400 kt burn. Do NOT read "the jet held 240 m" as an answer to the anchor's question:
# it held it over a PLANE.

# MEASURED (fingerprint 673753b8b0cf3f3e, exit 0): 0.85 METRES OVER 300 KILOMETRES - OVER A PLANE.
#   the hold      `altM` min 239.70 / max 240.55 / mean 240.002 over the 14,500 telemetry rows of the
#                 ingress leg (t <= 1,450 s). Under `--elev const` `aglM` is the same number, which is
#                 the disclosure and not a result
#   the bomb      `aimErrM=48.1096 aimLongM=38.8717 aimAcrossM=-28.3465`; `w2van` DESTROYED. The
#                 across-track half is seventeen times sortie 01's, because a 300 km Direct leg
#                 arrives with a lateral offset a 40 km one does not have
#   fuel          6,971.8 -> 5,078.9 lb over 300 km plus egress = 1,892.9 lb
#   ATTRIBUTION A4, THE ONE THAT ANSWERS THE HEADER'S QUESTION: this file re-run under
#   `--elev tiles --base http://localhost:8081` over the real Jordan and Iraq does not reach tick one -
#       `t=0.0 ERROR mission RESULT unit=w2vip2 result=FAIL reason="spawn altitude is below ground"
#        altM=240 groundM=487.48`
#   The anchor's LOWER disputed value is worse: the ground under this route reaches 1,599.22 m.
#   ATTRIBUTION A3, the 30 m half of the [DISPUTED] value, flown over the same 0 m plane: the guidance
#   holds it (`altM` min 29.02) and THE BOMB NEARLY DOES NOT ARM - `armMarginS=0.486341` against the
#   Mk-84's own 2.0 s arming time, 24 % of the delay left, with `aimErrM=44.3873`. So over a plane the
#   30 m variant is not a terrain-following problem, it is a FUZING problem; over the real ground
#   neither value is flyable at all. Both are carried, neither is preferred, and the campaign's arena
#   is the only reason 240 m is expressible.

unit w2vip2
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 32.20668 41.54287 240 68.4 400        # 300.0 km short of the dome, the raid's own bearing
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100                        # 6,972 lb internal, clean: this sortie is the leg only
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 33.20000 44.52000 240 400                # THE AIM POINT at the end of the 300 km leg
  wp 33.00132 43.92190 240 400                # egress, 60 km back down the inbound track
  objective survive

unit w2van
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 33.20000 44.52000 ground 68.4 0
